<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP copper production rises in Nov.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP copper production rises in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Tuesday that its production of copper in concentrate, copper cathodes and copper anodes rose in the six months ended November 30 compared with the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>The rise reflected the Phase Three expansion of its 57.5 percent owned La Escondida mine in Chile and the acquisition of Magma Copper Co last January, BHP said in its November production report.  </p>
<p>Copper in concentrate output from the Ok Tedi mine in Papua New Guinea (PNG) improved in November versus the year-ago level, but was down on a year-to-date basis due to lower mill throughput and recoveries and bad weather, BHP said.</p>
<p>Copper concentrate output rose 64 eprcent in November from November 1995, while year-to-date output was up 41 percent, it said.</p>
